    "mechanism": "In baseline data (raw_study_results.json), Optimized_ULC_v2 achieved P95 latency of 1.5141 ms, whereas MultiObjective_ULC_v3 achieved 1.6563 ms. Because P95 latency is an objective to minimize, ULC-v3 could not dominate ULC-v2 on baseline data. ULC-v2 was therefore non-dominated (N=8). In the reproduced run, CPU scheduling variation on Windows 11 caused ULC-v3 to run with a faster P95 latency (1.3259 ms) than ULC-v2 (1.4551 ms). Because ULC-v3 was superior or equal on all other 8 objectives, ULC-v3 strictly dominated ULC-v2 on reproduced data, dropping the count to N=7.",
    "scientific_resolution": "Hardware scheduling latency is physical and non-deterministic. Under invariant algorithmic metrics (excluding latency), ULC-v3 strictly dominates ULC-v2. Under the strict 9-objective protocol with measured latency, baseline data has 8 non-dominated configurations, and reproduced timing has 7 non-dominated configurations."
  },
